{"id": "jest_failure", "cmd": "npx jest --ci", "generator": "jest_failure", "params": {"suites": 60, "test_name": "Invoice › rounds totals to cents"}, "gate": "xfail", "phase": "S2", "filter_output": true, "checks": {"must_contain": ["$test_name", "$totals"]}, "tags": ["tests", "jest"], "why": "sixty PASS suites and one failure; today's filter keeps the totals but drops the '● name' block as non-error lines (measured 2026-09-04)"}
{"id": "binary_garbage", "cmd": "cat model.bin", "generator": "binary_garbage", "params": {"bytes": 2097152}, "gate": "must_pass", "phase": null, "filter_output": true, "checks": {}, "tags": ["binary", "budget", "regression-guard"], "why": "2 MB of random bytes decoded with errors=replace: one byte in 256 is a newline, so the filter fires and today's response is under budget (measured 2026-09-04); it must stay that way"}
{"id": "binary_single_line", "cmd": "cat texture.pak", "generator": "binary_garbage", "params": {"bytes": 2097152, "strip_newlines": true}, "gate": "xfail", "phase": "S1", "filter_output": true, "checks": {}, "tags": ["binary", "budget", "long-line"], "why": "the same 2 MB with no newline at all: the line-count trigger never fires and the whole blob reaches the agent"}
